README-ARCHIVERS -- the archivers, by format, and which to takeTake `tar' to pack your own things and `unzip' to open what other peoplesend.  `tar' is 22K, needs no Microware module, writes the format everyother system still reads, and is what unpacks this disk when it is built.`unzip' reads the format the rest of the world settled on.FORMATS-------  format         write             read only            needs cio  --------------------------------------------------------------------  ARC            arc, marc         --                   --  LHarc          lha, lharc        xlharc               --  zoo            zoo               booz, fiz            zoo, booz, fiz  tar            tar, gtar         --                   --  zip            zip               unzip, zipinfo,      unzip, zipinfo,                                   funzip               funzip  compress       compress, compr   --                   --  gzip           gzip              --                   --  shell archive  shar              unshar, sh           --  ar (library)   ar, ar2           --                   ar2`cio' is Microware's module.  It ships here, so on this disk it costsnothing; it is one more file to carry if you take a program away.DOC/README-CIO.THE FILES---------  file            bytes  cio  module    source          docs  ------------------------------------------------------------------  tar             22966  no   tar       SRC/eff_tar     DOC/tar  REBUILT/gtar   131060  no   gtar      SRC/gtar        DOC/gtar  zip             63972  no   zip       --              DOC/zip  unzip           42060  yes  unzip     SRC/unzip50     DOC/unzip  zipinfo         23904  yes  zipinfo   SRC/unzip50     DOC/zipinfo  lha             65560  no   LHa       SRC/lha208      DOC/lha  lharc           55816  no   lharc     SRC/forum17     DOC/lharc  xlharc          48878  no   xlharc    --              DOC/lharc  zoo             44926  yes  zoo       SRC/zoo     