t `.gz'.  CMDS/REBUILT also has gzip68k_csl,             gzip020_csl and gzipcpu32k_csl, for 68000, 68020 and CPU32,             each needing `csl'.  Take the plain `gzip' unless you know you             want one of those.  ar         you want a Unix-style object library.  OS-9's own libraries             are different things; see `liborder' and `unpacklib'.USING THEM----------None reads a configuration file or a termcap.They unpack into the current data directory, so `chd' where you want thefiles first.  For zip and unzip, stand in the directory and use bare namesat both ends: zip strips the leading slash from a pathname it stores, and`unzip -d <dir>' writes nothing and reports success.